Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/a5xx: release the shadow buffer CPU mapping on teardown

msm_gem_kernel_new() obtains an IOVA pin and a CPU mapping reference
for the shadow buffer. Dropping only the IOVA pin leaves vmap_count
and its page pin nonzero when the GEM object is freed. A controlled
GPU unbind then warns in msm_gem_vunmap and update_lru_locked.

Pair the allocation with msm_gem_kernel_put(), which releases the CPU
mapping reference, IOVA pin and GEM reference. Firmware buffers have
different mapping lifetimes and retain their existing teardown. No
rendering or PM-policy change.

---

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a5xx_gpu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a5xx_gpu.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a5xx_gpu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a5xx_gpu.c
@@ -1061,10 +1061,7 @@
 		drm_gem_object_put(a5xx_gpu->gpmu_bo);
 	}
 
-	if (a5xx_gpu->shadow_bo) {
-		msm_gem_unpin_iova(a5xx_gpu->shadow_bo, gpu->vm);
-		drm_gem_object_put(a5xx_gpu->shadow_bo);
-	}
+	msm_gem_kernel_put(a5xx_gpu->shadow_bo, gpu->vm);
 
 	adreno_gpu_cleanup(adreno_gpu);
 	kfree(a5xx_gpu);
